  "final_span": "honest or not. The answers were mixed. Forty-seven percent of Democrats stated they perceived their favored candidate as reliable. According to the poll, half of those identifying as Hispanic and one-quarter of Anglos viewed Cruz as honest, while slightly less than one-quarter of those identifying as Hispanic found O\u2019Rourke to be honest. Ipsos used a convenience sample of 1,005 self-identified \u201cadministered in English and Spanish\u201d in Texas, according to the poll. The poll was carried out between September 11 and 12. The modest sample size is characteristic of Ipsos online polls, as Jackson noted. But that\u2019s not to say \u201cthere won\u2019t be any error.\u201d The margin of error \u201ccould be plus or minus than margin of error,\u201d he said. While most online polls have larger-than-threshold margins of error, Ipsos\u2019 polls don\u2019t since 2017",
